{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7a1c3d2-9f45-4e18-a6b0-timechamp0001",
    "name": "Time Champ API (v1)",
    "description": "Time Champ backend — NestJS. Global prefix /api/v1 (health + metrics are excluded).\n\nAUTH: POST /auth/login sets httpOnly accessToken + refreshToken cookies. Postman's cookie jar picks them up automatically, so every later request just works. The login request also copies the token into the {{accessToken}} collection variable, so Bearer auth works too (the API accepts either).\n\nEnvelope: successful responses are { success: true, data }, errors are { success: false, error: { code, message } }.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "host", "value": "http://localhost:4000" },
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "{{host}}/api/v1" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "otherUserId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "companyId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "managerId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "notificationId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "screenshotId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "enrollToken", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Not behind the /api/v1 prefix and not guarded.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{host}}/health", "host": ["{{host}}"], "path": ["health"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Process metrics",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{host}}/metrics", "host": ["{{host}}"], "path": ["metrics"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const token = pm.cookies.get('accessToken');",
                  "if (token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', token); }",
                  "try {",
                  "  const user = pm.response.json().user;",
                  "  if (user && user.id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', user.id); }",
                  "} catch (e) { /* non-JSON response */ }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@timechamp.test\",\n  \"password\": \"admin123\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "200. Sets httpOnly accessToken + refreshToken cookies. Returns { user } only — the tokens are not in the body.\n\nFailure cases the client should distinguish:\n- 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS — 'Invalid email or password'. Unknown email OR wrong password; deliberately the same for both.\n- 403 ACCOUNT_DISABLED — 'Your account has been blocked. Contact your manager or an administrator.' Only returned once the password is correct, so it never reveals that a blocked account exists."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Enroll agent (password-less)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{enrollToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/enroll", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "enroll"] },
            "description": "200. Signs in using the enrollment token baked into a per-user agent download."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh tokens",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "refresh"] },
            "description": "Rotates the refresh cookie and issues a new access cookie. No body — reads the refreshToken cookie."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "logout"] },
            "description": "Revokes the refresh token and clears both cookies."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Users",
      "description": "JwtAuthGuard on the whole controller. Results are role-scoped inside the use cases.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&limit=20&sort=joined_desc",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "1" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "20" },
                {
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "joined_desc",
                  "description": "name_asc | name_desc | joined_asc | joined_desc | role_asc | role_desc. Defaults to joined_desc."
                },
                { "key": "search", "value": "", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "role", "value": "MANAGER", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "managerId", "value": "{{managerId}}", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Scope by role: SUPER_ADMIN/ADMIN see all, MANAGER sees their reports, USER sees only themselves. Returns { data, meta: { total, page, limit, totalPages } }. Every row includes `status`.\n\nSORT — pass one of six tokens as ?sort=, matching the UI labels:\n  name_asc     Name (A – Z)            firstName, then lastName\n  name_desc    Name (Z – A)\n  joined_desc  Joined Date (Newest)    default\n  joined_asc   Joined Date (Oldest)\n  role_asc     Role (A – Z)            see caveat\n  role_desc    Role (Z – A)\n\nAnything outside that list is a 400, so the client can't order by arbitrary columns.\n\nCAVEAT on role: role is a Postgres enum, so the database orders it by declaration order — SUPER_ADMIN, ADMIN, MANAGER, USER — i.e. seniority, NOT the alphabet. role_asc therefore returns SUPER_ADMIN first, not ADMIN. True alphabetical would need a raw-SQL cast.\n\nEvery ordering ends with a tiebreak on id so rows can't shuffle between pages."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get user detail",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "try {",
                  "  const u = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "  if (u && u.id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('otherUserId', u.id); }",
                  "} catch (e) { /* non-JSON response */ }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{otherUserId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{otherUserId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Every field of one user: id, email, firstName, lastName, name, role, department, designation, managerId, companyId, shiftId, shiftStart, shiftEnd, status, createdAt.\n\nVisibility: admins see anyone, a manager sees their reports and themselves, a plain user sees only themselves. Anything you may not view returns 'Unknown user' rather than 403, so ids can't be probed.\n\nPass your own id to read your own profile. Disabled users are returned normally — status is in the payload."
            }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update user",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"Jane\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Doe\",\n  \"designation\": \"Senior Team Lead\",\n  \"department\": \"Engineering\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{otherUserId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{otherUserId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Partial update — send only the fields you're changing; omitted fields are left alone. Returns the full updated user, same shape as Get user detail.\n\nEditable here: firstName, lastName, designation, department. Role, manager, company and shift are NOT editable through this route. Status has its own route (POST /users/:id/status).\n\nWho can edit: admins anyone, a manager their own reports (and themselves), a plain user only themselves."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create users (single or bulk)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"jane@acme.test\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Jane\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Doe\",\n  \"password\": \"S3curePass!\",\n  \"role\": \"MANAGER\",\n  \"department\": \"Engineering\",\n  \"designation\": \"Team Lead\",\n  \"companyId\": null,\n  \"shiftId\": null,\n  \"shiftStart\": \"10:00\",\n  \"shiftEnd\": \"19:00\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["users"] },
            "description": "201. Send one user at the top level (as shown), or bulk with { \"users\": [ {...}, {...} ] }. Returns { created: [...], errors: [{ email, error }] } — partial success is normal."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create users (bulk)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"users\": [\n    {\n      \"email\": \"a@acme.test\",\n      \"firstName\": \"Amy\",\n      \"lastName\": \"Adams\",\n      \"role\": \"USER\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"email\": \"b@acme.test\",\n      \"firstName\": \"Ben\",\n      \"lastName\": \"Brown\",\n      \"role\": \"USER\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["users"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Block user (status DISABLED)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"DISABLED\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{otherUserId}}/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{otherUserId}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "status is ACTIVE (unblock) or DISABLED (block) — those are the only two values the enum has.\n\nReturns the full user object, same shape as GET /users/:id, inside { success: true, data }.\n\nTakes effect immediately: every authenticated request re-reads status, and login / refresh / agent-enrollment all reject non-ACTIVE.\n\nIdempotent — blocking an already-blocked user succeeds quietly (no 409).\n\nWho can: admin anyone, manager their own reports only, plain user nobody. Blocking yourself is rejected. A target you may not touch returns 'Unknown user', not 403.\n\nRejected with a surfaceable message when the target is the last active admin."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Unblock user (status ACTIVE)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"ACTIVE\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{otherUserId}}/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{otherUserId}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Same endpoint, ACTIVE instead of DISABLED. The last-active-admin guard does not apply when unblocking."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete user (soft)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{otherUserId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{otherUserId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Soft delete. You cannot delete yourself."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
